    {
      "source": "The System property <code>file.encoding</code> is normally set by the JVM in response to the\n<code>LANG</code> or <code>LC_ALL</code> environment variables. It is used (along with other\nplatform-dependent variables keyed off those environment variables) to encode JVM\narguments as well as file names and paths. In most cases you can override the file\nencoding System property on the command line (with standard JVM features), but also\nconsider setting the <code>LANG</code> environment variable to an explicit\ncharacter-encoding value (e.g. \"en_GB.UTF-8\").",
      "translation": "`file.encoding` 系统属性通常由 JVM 根据 `LANG` 或 `LC_ALL` 环境变量进行设置。它用于（连同其他基于这些环境变量的平台相关变量）对 JVM 参数以及文件名和路径进行编码。在大多数情况下，您可以使用标准的 JVM 功能在命令行上覆盖文件编码系统属性，但也可以考虑将 `LANG` 环境变量设置为明确的字符编码值（例如 \"en_GB.UTF-8\"）。",
      "count": 2
    },
